WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:14.654
not fair!"

2
00:00:15.154 --> 00:00:15.914
cried Katie.

3
00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:20.796
"How can I be an Earthworm when I'm busy selling earthworms?"

4
00:00:22.097 --> 00:00:23.778
She kicked the big tub of ice.

5
00:00:23.798 --> 00:00:27.139
"Sorry, partner," said Luke.

6
00:00:27.659 --> 00:00:29.300
"You're in the bait business now."

7
00:00:30.392 --> 00:00:35.416
"But today is a perfect Saturday for scavenger hunting," said Katie.

8
00:00:35.436 --> 00:00:42.542
"Today is a perfect Saturday for fishing and selling fishing worms," Luke said.

9
00:00:43.663 --> 00:00:45.585
Katie stared across Main Street.

10
00:00:45.605 --> 00:00:47.526
"Look!" she said.

11
00:00:47.546 --> 00:00:50.849
"Scavengers at Pinker's Drugstore!

12
00:00:51.309 --> 00:00:52.991
And there go the Tornadoes!

13
00:00:53.671 --> 00:00:54.512
Oh, Luke!"

14
00:00:55.032 --> 00:00:55.693
she cried.

15
00:00:55.713 --> 00:00:58.996
"Everybody is getting ahead of us!"

16
00:01:00.616 --> 00:01:02.357
The Tornadoes had been busy.

17
00:01:02.377 --> 00:01:06.440
"A business card," Joy read from the list.

18
00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:08.181
"From Mr.

19
00:01:08.241 --> 00:01:10.823
Todd's barbershop," said Carlos.

20
00:01:11.383 --> 00:01:12.784
He dropped it in the bag.

21
00:01:12.804 --> 00:01:16.247
"A pen printed with a company name."

22
00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:20.229
"From Willow Creek Bank," said Laura.

23
00:01:20.249 --> 00:01:23.351
"A yard sale announcement."

24
00:01:23.371 --> 00:01:25.333
"Right here!"

25
00:01:25.813 --> 00:01:26.714
said Carlos.

26
00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:28.575
"Wait a minute.

27
00:01:29.015 --> 00:01:31.277
Let me see that," Laura said.

28
00:01:32.437 --> 00:01:34.079
She looked at the sheet of paper.

29
00:01:34.099 --> 00:01:37.641
"This sale is today—right now!"

30
00:01:38.302 --> 00:01:39.883
Laura loved yard sales.

31
00:01:39.903 --> 00:01:45.547
"But we're supposed to be hunting, not shopping," Carlos said, frowning.

32
00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:48.529
"That's true," said Joy.

33
00:01:48.549 --> 00:01:51.130
"We can hunt at the sale!"

34
00:01:51.671 --> 00:01:52.551
pleaded Laura.

35
00:01:52.571 --> 00:01:55.854
"That's true too," said Joy.

36
00:01:55.874 --> 00:01:58.415
"Please, please!"

37
00:01:59.544 --> 00:02:00.405
begged Laura.

38
00:02:01.426 --> 00:02:03.747
Carlos looked at Manny and sighed.

39
00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:05.328
"I give up."

40
00:02:06.429 --> 00:02:08.531
"Hooray!" cried Laura.

41
00:02:09.671 --> 00:02:13.054
The Tornadoes hopped on their bikes and headed up Main Street.

42
00:02:13.074 --> 00:02:15.596
"Hi, Katie!

43
00:02:15.976 --> 00:02:16.636
Hi, Luke!"

44
00:02:17.397 --> 00:02:20.339
they called as they flew past Fried Pie Heaven.

45
00:02:20.359 --> 00:02:22.641
"Where are you going?"

46
00:02:23.301 --> 00:02:24.102
yelled Katie.

47
00:02:25.263 --> 00:02:29.897
But the Tornadoes were gone—over the bridge and down County Road.

48
00:02:29.917 --> 00:02:32.599
"Follow the arrows!"

49
00:02:33.139 --> 00:02:36.301
called Laura, pointing to a big, pink sign.

50
00:02:37.442 --> 00:02:41.704
The Tornadoes passed Blackberry Road and then Cemetery Road.

51
00:02:42.865 --> 00:02:44.426
Laura saw another sign.

52
00:02:44.446 --> 00:02:45.746
"Turn here!"

53
00:02:46.847 --> 00:02:51.330
The Tornadoes went up a steep hill and then flew down the other side.

54
00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:55.432
"Whee!" screamed Manny.

55
00:02:56.764 --> 00:02:57.525
"There it is!"

56
00:02:58.125 --> 00:02:58.886
yelled Laura.

57
00:02:58.906 --> 00:03:00.947
"It's at the Stevensons' house."

58
00:03:02.228 --> 00:03:06.851
The Tornadoes' bikes screeched to a stop in the driveway of an old farmhouse.

59
00:03:08.092 --> 00:03:09.033
"Hello, Mrs.

60
00:03:09.053 --> 00:03:11.355
Stevenson!" they called.

61
00:03:12.556 --> 00:03:17.459
Mrs. Stevenson was in the yard, arranging dishes and glass jars on a table.

62
00:03:17.479 --> 00:03:19.601
"Hello, kids!"

63
00:03:20.041 --> 00:03:20.741
she answered.

64
00:03:20.761 --> 00:03:23.904
"Come see what we have—lots of treasures!"

65
00:03:25.184 --> 00:03:26.725
"Look at all this stuff!"

66
00:03:27.286 --> 00:03:28.006
said Laura.

67
00:03:29.187 --> 00:03:31.709
She grabbed a red hat with black feathers.

68
00:03:31.729 --> 00:03:34.150
"Only fifty cents!

69
00:03:34.691 --> 00:03:35.391
How do I look?"

70
00:03:35.872 --> 00:03:38.413
She put a big straw hat on Joy's head.

71
00:03:38.433 --> 00:03:40.715
"Perfect!" she said.

72
00:03:42.156 --> 00:03:43.617
Joy reached in her pocket.

73
00:03:43.637 --> 00:03:46.239
"I've got one dollar," she said.

74
00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:53.224
Clothes, blankets, and boxes of ribbons, lace, and buttons covered tables on the lawn.

75
00:03:54.292 --> 00:03:58.315
There were old tools, copper pots, and empty bottles.

76
00:03:59.516 --> 00:04:04.219
There was a typewriter, an umbrella, a saddle, and a sled.

77
00:04:04.239 --> 00:04:06.761
"Baseball cards!"

78
00:04:07.361 --> 00:04:08.101
said Manny.

79
00:04:09.562 --> 00:04:12.965
Carlos held up an old Willow Creek campaign button.

80
00:04:12.985 --> 00:04:16.187
"Horton for Mayor," he read.

81
00:04:16.207 --> 00:04:18.088
"Don't we need one of these?"

82
00:04:18.108 --> 00:04:21.150
"Yes!" said Laura.

83
00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:23.332
"I knew we'd find something here!"

84
00:04:24.532 --> 00:04:27.853
"Look at these old photos of Willow Creek," said Joy.

85
00:04:28.954 --> 00:04:30.635
Laura reached into the box.

86
00:04:30.655 --> 00:04:33.276
"A horse and buggy on Main Street!"

87
00:04:33.296 --> 00:04:36.537
"Hey," said Carlos.

88
00:04:36.997 --> 00:04:39.058
"This must be the old fire station."

89
00:04:40.158 --> 00:04:42.319
"Look at this one," said Joy.

90
00:04:42.819 --> 00:04:44.420
Laura looked over her shoulder.

91
00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:48.522
"It's a gravestone," Laura said.

92
00:04:48.542 --> 00:04:51.803
"Howard Lightfoot Jackson."

93
00:04:51.823 --> 00:04:55.080
"Look at the date on it," said Joy.

94
00:04:55.100 --> 00:05:01.144
"1848!" "That's older than the town," said Carlos.

95
00:05:01.164 --> 00:05:05.206
"That could be the oldest grave in Willow Creek!"

96
00:05:05.646 --> 00:05:06.327
said Joy.

97
00:05:06.347 --> 00:05:09.188
"We'll look for it at the cemetery."

98
00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:13.331
"I don't want to go to the cemetery!"

99
00:05:13.791 --> 00:05:14.692
Manny cried.

100
00:05:15.172 --> 00:05:16.152
He looked scared.

101
00:05:17.673 --> 00:05:20.435
Suddenly Joy felt a hand on her shoulder.

102
00:05:21.015 --> 00:05:21.695
It was Mrs.

103
00:05:21.755 --> 00:05:25.461
Stevenson. "The grave is not in the cemetery.

104
00:05:26.281 --> 00:05:29.062
It's older than the cemetery," she said.

105
00:05:29.082 --> 00:05:31.103
"Where is it, Mrs.

106
00:05:31.143 --> 00:05:32.944
Stevenson?" asked Joy.

107
00:05:32.964 --> 00:05:36.105
"It's right here on the farm.

108
00:05:36.626 --> 00:05:39.507
The Jacksons were the first family to settle here.

109
00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:44.029
It's on their family burial ground, down past the pasture.

110
00:05:44.569 --> 00:05:45.669
Would you like to see it?"

111
00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.251
"Yes, we would!"

112
00:05:48.831 --> 00:05:51.312
Joy, Carlos, and Laura said together.
